export const GUIDE = "## Getting started and finding your way\n(screen: dashboard)\n\nHotelEasy runs the whole hotel: front desk, billing, restaurant and bar, housekeeping, maintenance, stock, staff and reports. Everyone signs in with their own email, and sees only the parts their role allows.\n\n**Moving around.** The menu on the left lists the screens you can use, grouped as Front office, Food & beverage, Management, Operations and Admin. On a phone, tap the menu button at the top left. If something you need is missing from your menu, your role doesn't include it: ask the owner or a manager.\n\n**Several hotels.** If you work for more than one hotel, tap the hotel name at the top left to switch.\n\n**The bell** at the top right shows what needs attention now (late check-outs, guests waiting, requests not answered, the day not closed...). Tap an alert to go to the right screen.\n\n**First setup for a new hotel (owner or manager), in this order:**\n1. Settings & Team: hotel details, VAT and tourism levy, invoice settings, then invite your staff.\n2. Rooms: add room types (with the normal rate per night), then the rooms.\n3. Rates & seasons: weekends, high season, meal plans (optional).\n4. Restaurant & Bar POS → Setup: outlets, tables and menu (there is a \"Set up with sample menu\" button).\n5. Inventory (optional): stores and items, recipes for menu items.\n6. Staff & rota: add staff, pay rates, shift types.\n7. Online booking & reviews: switch on your booking page.\n\n**Signing in.** Staff get an email invitation from Settings & Team and sign up with that same email. \"Forgot password\" on the sign-in page sends a reset link.\n\n## Making and changing a reservation\n(screen: reservations)\n\n**New booking:** Reservations → **New reservation** (top right), or click an empty cell on the **Calendar** tab to book that room for that night.\n1. **Guest:** type a name or phone to find a returning guest, or choose **Add as new guest** and fill in the name and phone.\n2. **Check-in** and **Check-out** dates, **Adults** and **Children**.\n3. **Room type**, then a room, or **Assign later** (a room is chosen at check-in).\n4. **Meal plan** (Room only, Bed & breakfast, Half board...) if your hotel has plans.\n5. The price comes from Rates & seasons automatically. Changing it by hand needs the \"change the room rate\" permission; otherwise you see \"Season price. Ask a manager to change the rate.\" **Use season prices** puts the automatic price back.\n6. **Booked via** (walk-in, phone, website, Booking.com...), **Company account** if a company pays (choose **Who pays** and an **Order / LPO number**), and **Special requests**.\n7. Save. The booking gets a code like HE-ABC123.\n\n**Walk-in guest:** make the booking with today as check-in, then press **Check in** on it straight away.\n\n**Change a booking** (dates, room, guest, extend a stay): open it from the list and edit, then save. The price is worked out again for the new dates.\n\n**Finding a booking:** the tabs are **Arrivals**, **In house**, **Departures**, **Upcoming**, **Calendar** and **Search all**. The search box takes a guest name, phone, room or booking code.\n\n**Calendar tab:** bars start mid-day on arrival and end mid-day on departure. Click an empty cell to book that room.\n\n**Can't find a free room?** The room type is full for those nights. Try another room type or dates, or check the Calendar tab.\n\n## Checking a guest in\n(screen: reservations)\n\n1. Reservations → **Arrivals** tab (today's arrivals).\n2. Press **Check in** on the guest's row.\n3. Choose the **Room**. Only rooms of the booked type that are free for the whole stay are listed. If a room shows as dirty or under maintenance you get a warning: make sure it's ready first.\n4. Press **Check in** (green). The room becomes occupied, and the room nights start going onto the guest's bill.\n\n**Before or at check-in:**\n- If the guest did **online check-in**, their ID and signed registration card are already there: see Online check-in.\n- To print a **registration card** for signing: Online check-in → the guest → **Registration card**.\n- Take a deposit or payment from the bill: press **Bill** on the row (see Taking payments).\n\n**Guest arrived early or the room isn't ready:** check them in when the room is ready; Housekeeping shows the room as \"Urgent (guest arriving)\".\n\n**No Check in button?** Either the arrival date is in the future, or your role can't check guests in (ask a manager).\n\n## Checking a guest out and settling the bill\n(screen: reservations)\n\n1. Reservations → **Departures** (or **In house**) → press **Check out** on the guest.\n2. The bill opens. Check the charges with the guest (room nights, restaurant and bar items charged to the room, extras).\n3. If there is a balance, take the payment on the **Payments** tab (cash, M-Pesa, card...). The button shows \"Take KES … first\" until the bill is paid.\n4. Press **Check out & issue invoice**. The tax invoice is created and can be printed; the room goes to housekeeping for cleaning.\n\n**Company pays:** if the booking is billed to a company account, the company's share moves to the company's account at check-out, and the guest only pays their extras.\n\n**Guest leaves owing money** (credit agreed by a manager): a manager can use \"Check out with … owing\". It shows later under Billing → Open bills → \"Checked out, still owing\".\n\n**Leaving early:** check out on the day they leave; unused future nights are not charged.\n\n**Late check-out:** the bell shows guests past check-out time. Extend the booking, or add a late check-out charge on the bill with **Add to bill**.\n\n**No Check out button?** Your role may not be allowed to check guests out; ask a manager.\n\n## Guest bills, payments, refunds and invoices\n(screen: billing)\n\nOpen a guest's bill from Reservations (**Bill** button) or Billing & Payments → **Open bills**.\n\n**Take a payment or deposit:** Payments tab → choose the method (cash, M-Pesa, card, bank transfer...) → amount → reference → record it.\n- M-Pesa: send a pay prompt to the guest's phone (see M-Pesa), or tap \"Guest already paid? Type the M-Pesa code instead\" and type the 10-character code from their SMS (e.g. TK45ABC1XY). The same code can't be used twice.\n\n**Add a charge** (laundry, minibar, transfer, damage...): Charges → **Add to bill**: item, quantity, price.\n\n**Mistake?** Press **Void** on the charge or payment and give a reason. Front desk can undo their own entry within a few minutes; after that a manager or accountant voids it. Once the night audit has closed a day, that day's entries can't be voided: put a correction on today instead.\n\n**Refund:** Payments → **Refund to guest** (needs the refund permission).\n\n**Interim bill** (before check-out): **Print interim bill**. It says \"This is not a tax invoice\".\n\n**Bill a company:** **Move to company account** moves the balance to a company's account (see Company accounts).\n\n**Invoices:** created automatically at check-out. Billing & Payments → **Invoices** to find and reprint one.\n\n**Cash-up at the end of a shift:** Billing & Payments → **Payments & cash-up**: totals by method and **By staff member** for any period. Print it to check each cashier's drawer and M-Pesa.\n\n## M-Pesa pay prompts (STK push)\n(screen: billing)\n\nWhen M-Pesa prompts are switched on, you can send a payment request straight to the guest's phone. The guest enters their M-Pesa PIN and the payment records itself with the receipt number.\n\n**On a guest bill:** Bill → Payments → method M-Pesa → enter the amount → the guest's phone number (0712 345 678) → **Send prompt for KES …**. Wait for \"Paid … receipt …\". Amounts are whole shillings (rounded up).\n**At the POS:** Pay → M-Pesa tab → phone → **Send prompt**. The bill closes when paid.\n**Online guests** can pay the first night or whole stay from their booking page, if the hotel allows it.\n\n**\"The guest cancelled the prompt\" / \"didn't answer in time\":** just send it again. Check the phone is on, has M-Pesa, and enough balance.\n**\"Stop waiting\":** stops watching. If the guest pays anyway, it is still recorded.\n**Guest paid to the till or paybill directly:** type the M-Pesa code instead.\n\n**Setting it up (owner or manager):** Settings & Team → **M-Pesa prompts**: choose Test or Live, Paybill or Till, enter the number, the Daraja consumer key, secret and passkey, **Test the keys**, then switch **Use M-Pesa prompts** on. Live keys come from Safaricom after the hotel's Lipa na M-Pesa Online application.\n\n## Restaurant & Bar POS: taking orders and payment\n(screen: pos)\n\n**Start of shift:** Restaurant & Bar POS → **Open shift**, count your float (opening cash). You can take orders without a shift, but not payments.\n\n**Take an order:**\n1. Choose the outlet (Restaurant, Bar, Room service, Pool bar...) at the top.\n2. Tap a table, or **Walk-in / takeaway** (name optional), or a checked-in **Guest**.\n3. Tap menu items to add them (use the search box). Items with options ask \"How cooked?\", extras, etc. Add a **Note for the kitchen** if needed.\n4. Send the order: items go to the kitchen or bar screen.\n\n**Get paid:** press **Pay**. Choose **Cash** (enter cash received; change is shown), **M-Pesa** (send a prompt, or type the code), **Card**, or **Room** to charge it to a checked-in guest's room bill (search by room number or name and confirm with the guest). **Split evenly** splits between people; pay part with one method and the rest with another.\n\n**Bill menu** (the ⋯ button on the bill):\n- **Split items to new bill**, **Move to another table**, **Change number of guests**.\n- **Discount** and **Service charge**: need the discount permission, or a manager types their PIN.\n- **Void** an item (removes it, shows on the voids report) or **Comp** (free of charge). Food already sent to the kitchen needs a manager's approval.\n- **Void whole bill**.\n- **Board meal**: for guests on a meal plan, covers their included meal.\n\n**Receipt:** after paying press **Receipt** to print.\n\n**End of shift:** POS → your shift → **Close shift**: count all cash in the drawer (with the float) and enter it. The Z report shows expected cash and over/short. Print it and hand in the cash.\n\n**\"Open your cash shift before taking payment\"**: open a shift first. **\"Send or remove unsent items\"**: send the new items to the kitchen first.\n\n## POS setup: menu, prices, tables, kitchen screen, approval PIN\n(screen: pos)\n\nRestaurant & Bar POS → **Setup** (managers):\n- **Menu items:** add or edit an item: name, category, price (including tax), **Goes to** kitchen or bar, which outlets sell it, options, VAT. Mark **sold out** for today or hide it. **Recipe** links ingredients for stock and food cost.\n- **Categories**, **Options (modifiers)** such as \"How cooked?\" or \"Extras\" with extra prices.\n- **Outlets & service charge:** each outlet has its own tables, bills and sales report.\n- **Tables:** add tables per outlet (room service and takeaway don't need tables).\n\n**Approval PIN:** managers set a 4–6 digit PIN (POS → **Set PIN** or Setup → Your approval PIN). They type it on a waiter's screen to approve voids and discounts.\n\n**Kitchen & bar screen:** open \"Kitchen & bar screen\" on a tablet in the kitchen. Choose the station (kitchen or bar) and outlet. Tap an order to move it from new → preparing → ready. Use full screen.\n\n**Sales report:** POS → **Sales**: sales by outlet, payment, waiter, top items, tax, and every void, comp and discount with who approved it.\n\n## Guest profiles\n(screen: guests)\n\nGuests holds everyone who has booked or stayed, with their stays and spending.\n- **Add guest**, or guests are created when you make a booking.\n- Search by name, phone, email or ID number. Open a guest to see stays, **Completed stays** and **Room revenue**, then **Edit**.\n- Fields: name, phone, email, **ID type** and **ID / passport number**, nationality, date of birth, address, **Notes / preferences** (e.g. \"Prefers ground floor, allergic to nuts\") and **VIP guest**.\n- Deleting a guest needs a manager.\n\n## Online check-in and registration cards\n(screen: online-checkin)\n\nEvery confirmed booking has its own online check-in link. The guest fills in their ID or passport, trip details and other guests, reads the house rules and signs on their phone.\n\n**Send the link:** Online check-in → **WhatsApp**, or Reservations → the booking's menu → **Send online check-in (WhatsApp)** or **Copy online check-in link**. Best a day or two before arrival.\n**When the guest has filled it in:** Online check-in → **Review**: compare \"From the guest\" with \"On file now\", then **Accept details** or **Accept and check in**.\n**Registration card:** **Registration card** opens the signed card to print (Kenyan law requires a guest register). Reception checks the ID on arrival.\n**House rules** shown on the card: edit them at the bottom of Online check-in (managers).\n\n## Guest requests and room QR codes\n(screen: requests)\n\nGuests scan the QR code in their room and ask for towels, cleaning, a repair, a taxi, a wake-up call and more. Requests appear live in **Guest requests** with a sound, for the right team.\n- Press **Send** / **Done** as you handle it, and **Reply** to tell the guest (they see it on their phone). Requests waiting over 15 minutes are highlighted.\n- A guest phoned or asked at the desk? **Log a request**.\n- Repairs also open a maintenance ticket automatically.\n- **Setup & QR codes** (managers): **Print QR codes** for the rooms, choose **What guests can ask for** and which team gets each, and **Good to know** (Wi-Fi password, breakfast hours…) shown to guests.\n\n## Housekeeping: cleaning rooms\n(screen: housekeeping)\n\nRooms appear here automatically when a guest checks out. **Urgent (guest arriving)** shows rooms needed for today's arrivals first.\n- **My rooms** shows tasks assigned to you; **Everyone** shows all.\n- Tap **Start** when you begin a room and **Done** when it's ready. The room becomes available to sell. **Undo start** if you tapped by mistake.\n- Found a problem? **Report a problem** (sends it to maintenance).\n- Supervisors: **Add task** (deep clean, extra bed, VIP amenities…) and **Assign to** a housekeeper; **Daily service for occupied rooms** creates the day's stay-over cleaning.\n\n## Maintenance: reporting and fixing problems\n(screen: maintenance)\n\n**Report a problem** (anyone): Maintenance → **Report problem**, or from a room on the Rooms screen. Choose the room or place, what's wrong, how urgent, and tick **Room can't be used until fixed** if it can't be sold. Maintenance sees it straight away.\n**Fixing it** (maintenance staff and managers): open the issue, set **Status**, **Priority**, **Assigned to**, and write **What was done**. When fixed, an out-of-service room goes to housekeeping for cleaning before it can be sold again.\nTabs: **Open**, **Mine**, **Fixed**, **All**; **Rooms out of service** lists rooms that can't be sold.\n\n## Rooms, room types, prices, seasons and meal plans\n(screen: rates)\n\n**Rooms** (managers): **Room types** first (name, **Rate / night**, max guests, amenities), then **Add room** (number, floor, type). Each room shows live status; **Set status** marks clean/dirty. **Report a problem** sends it to maintenance.\n\n**Rates & seasons:**\n- **Rate calendar**: the price of each room type every night. \"Booking page prices\" shows online prices.\n- **Seasons** → **New season**: name, colour, first and last night, which nights of the week (a weekend uplift = Fri and Sat nights), **Change normal rates by (%)** and/or a fixed price per room type, **Minimum stay**, **No arrivals (online)**, and **Priority** (Normal for weekends, Higher for seasons, Highest for holidays, so Christmas beats a weekend inside it). Existing bookings keep their prices.\n- **Meal plans & packages** → **New plan**: Bed & breakfast, Half board, Full board or a package with extras; price per person per night; whether it's offered online.\n- **Meal counts**: how many breakfasts, lunches and dinners plan guests have each day (for the kitchen).\n\n## Company accounts (corporate clients, NGOs, government)\n(screen: companies)\n\nFor businesses that book now and pay later.\n- **Add company**: name, KRA PIN, contact, **Pays within (days)**, **Credit limit**, what they **Usually pay for** (everything or the room only), and **Negotiated rates** (a discount or a fixed rate per room type).\n- When booking, choose the **Company account**, **Who pays** and the **Order / LPO number**. At check-out the company's share moves to their account.\n- **Payment received** (or **Credit note**, **Extra charge**) records what they pay. **Print statement** for any period. **Ageing (CSV)** shows how long amounts have been owed.\n- Over the credit limit, a manager has to approve.\n\n## Online booking page, guest emails and reviews\n(screen: online)\n\n**Booking page:** Online booking & reviews → **Setup**: switch it on, set the page address, headline, about text, photo, WhatsApp number, cancellation days, minimum/maximum nights, payment instructions and house rules. **Rooms offered online** and online prices. Share the link (**Copy booking link**) on Google, Instagram, Facebook and WhatsApp, or add the **Book now** button to your website.\n**Online bookings** arrive in Reservations marked \"Website\", without a room: assign one at check-in.\n**Guests** can look up, change or cancel their booking with the code and their email or last name, check in online, and pay a deposit by M-Pesa if allowed.\n**Reviews:** after check-out, **Ask for feedback** sends each guest their private link. Read scores and comments, **Reply**, and choose which reviews show on the booking page.\n**Guest emails:** confirmation and pre-arrival emails (once email sending is set up for HotelEasy).\n\n## Booking.com & Airbnb calendar sync\n(screen: channels)\n\nEach calendar link connects one room to one listing, so the same night isn't sold twice.\n- **Add calendar link** (managers): choose the site and the room, paste the site's calendar export link. Then copy **our** link (copy button) into the site's calendar import. **How to connect** has the steps for Airbnb and Booking.com.\n- Bookings from the site arrive within about 10 minutes (or press **Sync now**) as reservations named \"Airbnb guest\" / \"Booking.com guest\" with price 0. At check-in, add the real name and the price (the site collects the money).\n- If the site cancels, the booking is cancelled here too.\n- **Double booked** (red): the room was already taken. The site's booking is kept without a room: move one of the guests to another room, and close the dates on the site.\n- Booking.com calendar sync only works when each room is its own room type (one unit).\n\n## Night audit and closing the day\n(screen: audit)\n\nClose each day once it's over (usually at night, or first thing the next morning).\n1. Night audit opens on the next day to close. Fix anything under **checks**: guests who should have arrived (check in or mark **No-show**), guests past check-out, open bills and cash shifts (warnings).\n2. Add **Notes for the manager** (e.g. power cut, noisy guests).\n3. Press **Close**. That day's payments, charges and restaurant bills are locked; corrections go on the next day.\n**Manager's report:** each closed day has a printable daily report: occupancy, ADR, RevPAR, revenue, money taken by method, balances, cash shifts and notes.\n**Reopen** (owner or manager): only the latest closed day, with a reason.\n**Error \"DAY_CLOSED\" / day is closed:** you're trying to change something on a closed day; post a correction today instead, or ask a manager to reopen.\n\n## Inventory: stock, receiving, transfers, counts, purchase orders\n(screen: inventory)\n\n**Set up:** Inventory → \"Set up stores and starter items\" creates Main store, Kitchen, Bar and Housekeeping stores. Link POS outlets to the store they take stock from.\n- **Stock**: every item with quantity per store, reorder level and value. **Low stock** filter, and **Draft purchase order** from low items.\n- **Receive goods**: from a purchase order or not, into a store, with the supplier's invoice number; optionally add the supplier's bill to Bills to pay.\n- **Transfer / issue**: move stock between stores, or issue to a department. **Record waste** for spoilt or broken items.\n- **Purchase orders**: **New order** → **Approve** (manager) → print/send → **Receive**.\n- **Counts**: **Start a count**, enter what's on the shelf, **Post count** (manager PIN). Stock is corrected.\n- **Recipes** (POS Setup → item → Recipe): ingredients come out of the outlet's store when items are sent to the kitchen or bar. **Costs** shows food cost % and margins.\n- **History**: every stock change; nothing can be edited.\n\n## Staff, rota, clock in, leave and payroll\n(screen: staff)\n\n**Staff & rota** (managers):\n- **Staff**: everyone who works here, with or without a login. **Add team logins** brings in invited users; add guards, gardeners and casuals without logins. Pay type (monthly, per day, per hour), allowances, KRA PIN, NSSF, SHA numbers, paid by M-Pesa/bank/cash.\n- **Rota**: click a day to add a shift; **Copy to next week**; publish so staff see it.\n- **Today**: who's on duty and who's late. **Clock in** staff without the app; correct clock times (with a reason).\n- **Leave**: approve requests or **Record leave**.\n- **Hours & pay**: hours worked, overtime, absent days, pay estimate, CSV for payroll.\n- **Payroll**: pick the month → **Refresh from time clock** → check → **Approve** → **Mark paid** (adds wages as an expense and PAYE, NSSF, SHIF, housing levy as bills due on the 9th) → **Payslips** to print. **Tax rates** holds the statutory rates.\n**My shifts** (everyone): your rota, **Clock in** / **Clock out**, **Ask for leave**, **My payslips**.\n\n## Expenses, bills to pay, profit & loss and reports\n(screen: finance)\n\n**Expenses & profit:**\n- **Expenses**: add what you spend (date, paid to, category, amount, VAT if you have an eTIMS invoice, paid or unpaid with due date). Tick \"Repeats every month\" for rent, salaries, internet; copy them into the new month.\n- **Bills to pay**: unpaid supplier bills, earliest due first: **Mark paid** with the M-Pesa/bank reference.\n- **Profit & loss** by month, with VAT and levy estimates. **Budget** per line. **Categories**.\n**Reports**: occupancy, ADR, RevPAR, revenue by department, tax summary, payments by method, where bookings come from, nationalities, unpaid guest bills, for any period. Print, or download CSV (needs the download permission).\n**Owner overview**: all your hotels on one page: revenue today, month to date, occupancy, collected, owed, bills due and alerts.\n\n## Settings, inviting staff, roles and permissions\n(screen: settings)\n\n**Settings & Team** (owner and managers):\n- **Hotel details**: name, address, phone, check-in and check-out times, VAT %.\n- **Team** → **Invite someone**: their email and role. They sign up with that email and get access. Change a person's role from the list, or remove them.\n- **Billing & invoices**: KRA PIN, tourism levy %, invoice prefix and number, M-Pesa paybill/till and bank details shown on invoices, invoice footer.\n- **M-Pesa prompts**: see the M-Pesa guide.\n**Built-in roles**: Owner (everything), Manager, Front desk, Housekeeping, Restaurant, Accountant, Maintenance, Storekeeper.\n**Roles & permissions** (owner only): **New role** makes a custom role (e.g. \"Night auditor\"): pick a job type, start from a built-in role, and tick exactly what it can view, create, edit and delete, plus special rights (refunds, voids, discounts, close the day, change room rates, download spreadsheets…). Give it to people in Settings & Team. **Who can do this?** shows everyone who has a permission.\nIf a screen or button is missing for someone, their role doesn't include it.\n\n## Common messages and what to do\n(screen: dashboard)\n\n- **\"You don't have permission\" / a button is missing**: your role doesn't allow it. Ask the owner or a manager, or ask them to do it.\n- **Day is closed (DAY_CLOSED)**: night audit locked that day. Put the correction on today, or ask a manager to reopen the day.\n- **\"You can't change the room rate\"**: only people with the room-rate permission can override season prices.\n- **\"Open your cash shift before taking payment\"** (POS): POS → Open shift.\n- **\"Send or remove unsent items before taking payment\"** (POS): send the new items first.\n- **M-Pesa code already used**: that payment is recorded already; check Payments.\n- **No room free / Sold out**: the room type is full for those nights; try other dates or types, or the Calendar tab.\n- **Room marked dirty at check-in**: ask housekeeping to finish it (Housekeeping → Start / Done).\n- **The page looks out of date**: refresh the browser. Check your internet connection.\n\n## WhatsApp bot and inbox\n(screen: whatsapp)\n\nGuests write to the hotel's WhatsApp number and the bot answers. Choose the bot in Setup:\n- **Menu bot (free):** a menu with buttons: **Rooms & prices**, **Check availability** (the guest sends dates like *20/12 to 22/12, 2 guests*), **My booking** (found by the guest's WhatsApp number, or the booking code and last name), **Location & contact** and **Talk to staff**. Guests can also reply 1–5 or type simple words in English or Swahili. Only HotelEasy's data is used; no AI and no extra cost.\n- **Smart bot (AI):** understands free questions and your extra facts. Needs the Anthropic key (paid per use); without it the menu bot answers.\n\n**Inbox:** WhatsApp → **Inbox**. Chats marked **Person** need a reply from your team (filter **Need a person**). Open a chat and type your reply; press Enter to send.\n**Take over / Let the bot answer:** when you take over (or simply reply), the bot stays quiet in that chat. Click **Let the bot answer** to hand it back. If the guest writes *menu*, *hi* or *habari* and nobody from the team has replied for 30 minutes, the bot takes the chat back by itself.\n**\"Reply window closed\":** WhatsApp only allows a free reply within 24 hours of the guest's last message. Wait until the guest writes again.\n**Free replies this month:** Meta gives each WhatsApp number 1,000 free replies a month. With **Stop at the free limit** on, nothing is sent after that until next month, so there is no charge. HotelEasy never starts chats or sends templates (those are always charged).\n**The bot doesn't answer:** check WhatsApp is on and the bot is switched on in Setup, the chat isn't taken over, this month's free replies aren't used up, and the booking page is on (Online → Setup).\n\n**Setting it up (owner or manager):** WhatsApp → **Setup**:\n1. From your Meta app (WhatsApp → API Setup) enter the **Phone number ID**, a permanent **access token** and the **app secret**.\n2. Copy the **Callback URL** and **Verify token** into Meta (WhatsApp → Configuration → Webhook), verify, and subscribe to **messages**.\n3. Choose **Menu bot (free)** or **Smart bot (AI)**, choose the free-limit setting, switch WhatsApp on and **Save**.\nEach hotel connects its own number; one hotel's chats and information are never shown to another.\n\n## Table QR codes and waiter calls (restaurant)\n(screen: tableqr)\n\nEach restaurant table has its own QR code. A diner scans it with their phone camera (no app, no sign-in) and sees the menu with prices, plus three buttons: **Call waiter**, **Bring the bill** (they choose cash, card or M-Pesa) and **Water / other** (with a short note).\n- Open **Table QR & waiter calls**. A table that calls turns **red with a \"!\"** and a sound plays (\"T3 · Bill · M-Pesa · 2 min\"). Tap **On my way** (the diner's phone shows \"On the way\"), then **Done**. Blue = someone is on the way.\n- **My outlets** (top of the page, saved on each phone or tablet): choose the outlets you serve, e.g. only **Bar**. You then see and hear only those tables. Tables waiting in other outlets still show in a small banner (**Show and help**), and if nobody answers one for **3 minutes** it rings on every device, so no table is forgotten (you can switch that off in My outlets).\n- Every waiter of an outlet gets the alert; whoever taps **On my way** first takes it. Everyone then sees who is going (\"Ravi is on the way\"; \"You're on the way\" on your own phone). If it isn't marked **Done** within 5 minutes, the tile says \"not done yet?\".\n- Keep the page open on a phone, tablet or the POS screen. Use **Sound on/off** at the top; the sound repeats while a table has waited over 2 minutes.\n- One open call per table: if the diner taps again, the same call is updated (e.g. from \"Waiter\" to \"Bill\").\n- **Setup** (managers): **Print QR codes** (all, or one outlet), switch Table QR on/off for a whole outlet or a single table, and **New code** if a sticker is copied or lost (the old one stops working).\n- **Response times** (managers): calls, average time to answer and to finish, calls that waited over 5 minutes, by outlet, request and staff member.\n- Tables and the menu come from **Restaurant & Bar POS → Setup**. Sold-out items show as sold out.\n- **Order from the phone** (switch it on per outlet in **Setup**; off by default): diners add dishes and send the order. It shows on the map in **violet** with a sound. Tap **Confirm** to put it on the table's POS bill and send it to the kitchen, or **Refuse** with a reason the diner sees. Prices always come from the menu. Dishes that need a choice (e.g. how the steak is cooked) are ordered through the waiter.\n- **Pay by M-Pesa from the phone** (per outlet in **Setup**; needs M-Pesa set up in Settings): diners see their bill and get an M-Pesa prompt. The payment goes on the bill automatically, in the shift of the waiter who opened it.\n- **Food from the kitchen to the table**: when the kitchen or bar screen marks dishes **Ready**, the table turns **green** with a sound (\"Table T3: food ready to serve\"). Collect the food and tap **Served** on the tile. Tiles also show what the kitchen is still making (\"Kitchen: 1 waiting · 2 preparing\").\n- The diner's phone follows each dish live: **Waiting for the kitchen/bar → Being prepared → Ready, coming to you → Served**, then \"Everything is served — enjoy your meal!\". If a dish takes over 25 minutes, the diner is offered \"Call waiter\" for an update.\n- Nothing here sends WhatsApp or SMS messages.";
